    "notes": "American put priced by Longstaff-Schwartz least-squares Monte Carlo (the `lsm` AST node): a post-run BACKWARD induction over the stored [dates x paths] time_history panel. At each exercise date the discounted future value is regressed (shared covariance regression) on a cubic basis of S over in-the-money paths; exercise where intrinsic > fitted continuation. Each path's discounted-to-t0 cashflow is injected per realization, so american_put's mean is the price (~6.04, vs binomial 6.09; in-sample low bias). The European put on the same path (euro_put) matches Black-Scholes and the American price exceeds it by the early-exercise premium. See AMERICAN_OPTION_EXAMPLE.md / AMERICAN_OPTION_SCOPE.md."
